    description: "**Origin.** Filed 2026-05-30 from the unlinked-investigation campaign (`~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/unlinked_investigation_TODO.md` Phase 6.2). The investigation identified two structural fix candidates that each close a cluster of unlinked items. User decision: do **A first, then B**. This WI exists so that the trial is queryable in `tracker ready` once code-change authorization opens; it is the meta-work-item for executing the two structural fixes.\n\n**Currently blocked on code-change authorization** (user is not yet ready for code changes in this workstream as of filing).\n\n## Sub-task A — `ClaimVerdict.inconclusive`\n\n**Closes:** INV-bitig (P0 Severe) + INV-gobob (P1, sibling in INV-fabov cluster) + INV-mofih (P1) + INV-nufob (P2). 4 items.\n\n**Fix shape.** Add a third verdict enum value `inconclusive` to `ClaimVerdict`. Refactor every check site at `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/verify_claims.py:229-291` so it returns `inconclusive` rather than falling through to `confirmed` when the underlying data is missing or malformed (empty source dir, broken YAML, gitleaks binary acting as no-op, taint catalog unoverridable). CLI exit-code mapping: `confirmed → 0`, `not_confirmed → 1`, `inconclusive → 2`.\n\n**Trial procedure.**\n1. Build a fixture with deliberately-broken inputs (empty source dir, malformed YAML claims file, gitleaks v8.30+ for the `--pipe` no-op case).\n2. Run `hypergumbo verify-claims` against each broken-input case.\n3. Confirm each emits `inconclusive` (not `confirmed`).\n4. Re-run dogfood self-analysis on hypergumbo's own codebase; confirm the 4 findings drop out of `bm.json`.\n\n**Time estimate.** ~½–1 day. One enum + ~10 check sites + tests.\n\n**Risk.** Behavior change visible to any caller relying on `--exit-code 0` as \"passed.\" But the current behavior IS the wrong answer — that's why it's a P0/Severe false-positive.\n\n**Payoff.** 4 items close. Real security correctness improvement.\n\n## Sub-task B — `AnalysisRun.create()` writer-contract property test\n\n**Targets:** Every member of INV-luhur (META: AnalysisRun writer contract) — 10+ members at filing time. Test is the gate; per-member writer-side fixes are downstream small PRs.\n\n**Fix shape.** Add `tests/test_behavior_map_writer_contract.py` (or analogous module location) wired to a fresh `bm.json` produced during CI. Each of the four sub-patterns in the INV-luhur description becomes its own assertion class:\n1. Schema-declares-no-writer: every dataclass field with a populated channel exists for every record.\n2. Default-only initializer: writer-side initialization-defaults never reach output.\n3. Same-name two-definitions: named summary metrics agree across serialization paths.\n4. Writer-writes-constant: emitters that populate evidence-derived slots use the derivation function not a constant.\n\n**Trial procedure.**\n1. Write the test.\n2. Run against `/tmp/hg-dogfood-s11/bm.json`.\n3. Confirm test fails today with at least one assertion per sub-pattern, matching the INV-luhur member set.\n4. Land the test in CI. Each subsequent failing member becomes its own writer-side PR gated by the test.\n\n**Time estimate.** ~½ day for the test itself. Writer-side fixes are downstream.\n\n**Risk.** Test is a gate, not a fix. It surfaces the problems but doesn't close items by itself. To close the INV-luhur member set, each writer needs its own small patch.\n\n**Payoff.** 10+ items become testable; future regressions get caught automatically.\n\n## Ordering rationale\n\nA first because: (a) closes higher-severity items (P0 + P1s) versus B's P1s; (b) demonstrates the methodology pays off in concrete closings within a day; (c) the verify-claims subcommand is the security-evidence layer — correctness gain is user-visible.\n\nB second because: (a) test-as-gate pattern is more durable but doesn't close items immediately; (b) once A demonstrates that trial-and-close works, B generalizes the approach to a different META.\n\n## Verification at trial close\n\nFor A: re-run `/tmp/active_audit/extract_refs3.py` against the active set; confirm INV-bitig, INV-gobob, INV-mofih, INV-nufob are no longer `violated`.\n\nFor B: confirm the new test fires on stale `bm.json` and passes against a fresh one after each writer-side fix lands."  # 3a0e
